2c:["$","p","OIST’s FAQ asks applicants to research faculty interests and availability, and to refrain from seeking faculty approval or support before applying. Use the published application and lab-matching process; a unit-fit worksheet is not a reason to solicit an unofficial offer.",{"children":"OIST’s FAQ asks applicants to research faculty interests and availability, and to refrain from seeking faculty approval or support before applying. Use the published application and lab-matching process; a unit-fit worksheet is not a reason to solicit an unofficial offer."}]
2d:["$","p","The following is an original fictional exercise, not a description of an OIST project or a successful applicant. A student has cleaned environmental sensor data in a university project. They want to understand how measurement noise affects a model. Their next step is to find a unit whose published work actually addresses that kind of question, rather than claim experience with an unfamiliar instrument.",{"children":"The following is an original fictional exercise, not a description of an OIST project or a successful applicant. A student has cleaned environmental sensor data in a university project. They want to understand how measurement noise affects a model. Their next step is to find a unit whose published work actually addresses that kind of question, rather than claim experience with an unfamiliar instrument."}]
2e:[["$","p",null,{"className":"table-scroll-hint","children":"On a small screen, scroll the table sideways to compare all columns."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-table-wrap","role":"region","aria-label":"Build a unit-fit worksheet from evidence you can explain","tabIndex":0,"children":["$","table",null,{"className":"guide-table","children":[["$","caption",null,{"children":"Build a unit-fit worksheet from evidence you can explain"}],["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[[["$","th","Worksheet field",{"scope":"col","children":"Worksheet field"}],["$","th","What the fictional student writes",{"scope":"col","children":"What the fictional student writes"}],["$","th","What still needs evidence",{"scope":"col","children":"What still needs evidence"}]],"$undefined"]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Prior work"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"Cleaned a small sensor dataset for a course"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"A genuine project report and the student’s actual contribution"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","1",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Learning question"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"How does measurement noise affect inference?"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"A current unit project that fits that question"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","2",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Method gap"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"Need supervised training in a specified analysis method"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"Whether that training is realistic in the placement"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","3",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Availability"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"Proposed uninterrupted placement dates"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"Home approval, unit availability and OIST’s selection"}]],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}]}],"$undefined"]
2f:["$","aside",null,{"className":"worked-example","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Worked example"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"If no unit’s published work fits your stated question, revise the shortlist or learning goal. Do not invent a project agreement, publication, skill or supervisor response."}]]}]
30:["$","section","3-Prepare documents and unlock the referee dependency",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-4","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Prepare documents and unlock the referee dependency"}],[["$","p","The application page lists academic records, statement, CV, references and identification/photo requirements. It specifies a statement limit of 250 words and 1,500 characters. At least one eligible recommendation must be received in the system before submission; applicants do not upload it on the referee’s behalf. The published application fee is ¥5,000 and non-refundable.",{"children":"The application page lists academic records, statement, CV, references and identification/photo requirements. It specifies a statement limit of 250 words and 1,500 characters. At least one eligible recommendation must be received in the system before submission; applicants do not upload it on the referee’s behalf. The published application fee is ¥5,000 and non-refundable."}],["$","p","A practical preparation order is to confirm a suitable referee first, then review each file against the live form. Save your own final draft privately. Distinguish “requested”, “received”, “uploaded” and “submitted” in your tracker so that a completed-looking folder does not hide an unmet dependency.",{"children":"A practical preparation order is to confirm a suitable referee first, then review each file against the live form. Save your own final draft privately. Distinguish “requested”, “received”, “uploaded” and “submitted” in your tracker so that a completed-looking folder does not hide an unmet dependency."}]],["$","ol",null,{"className":"process-steps","aria-label":"Prepare documents and unlock the referee dependency","children":[["$","li","Record the selected round, proposed dates and home-institution approval task.",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"children":1}],["$","strong",null,{"children":"Record the selected round, proposed dates and home-institution approval task."}]]}],["$","li","Prepare the academic file, current CV and a statement grounded in real work.",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"children":2}],["$","strong",null,{"children":"Prepare the academic file, current CV and a statement grounded in real work."}]]}],["$","li","Invite the eligible referee through the official process; inspect the received indicator.",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"children":3}],["$","strong",null,{"children":"Invite the eligible referee through the official process; inspect the received indicator."}]]}],["$","li","Check the live limits, identity instructions and fee step.",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"children":4}],["$","strong",null,{"children":"Check the live limits, identity instructions and fee step."}]]}],["$","li","Review the full application, submit through OIST and retain confirmation.",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"children":5}],["$","strong",null,{"children":"Review the full application, submit through OIST and retain confirmation."}]]}]]}],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
31:["$","section","4-Budget for support without treating every day as a paid working day",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-5","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Budget for support without treating every day as a paid working day"}],[["$","p","The programme description lists an allowance of ¥2,400 per working day, a direct return flight, furnished accommodation, shuttle access and administrative support. Support is for the intern, not accompanying dependants. Confirm the actual award and travel arrangements rather than buying travel on the basis of this summary.",{"children":"The programme description lists an allowance of ¥2,400 per working day, a direct return flight, furnished accommodation, shuttle access and administrative support. Support is for the intern, not accompanying dependants. Confirm the actual award and travel arrangements rather than buying travel on the basis of this summary."}],["$","p","For an original arithmetic exercise only, 20 paid working days at that allowance would equal ¥48,000. This is not a guaranteed monthly amount: calendar months contain different working-day patterns. Keep personal spending, payment timing and any dependent costs outside the confirmed support until OIST answers them.",{"children":"For an original arithmetic exercise only, 20 paid working days at that allowance would equal ¥48,000. This is not a guaranteed monthly amount: calendar months contain different working-day patterns. Keep personal spending, payment timing and any dependent costs outside the confirmed support until OIST answers them."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined",["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Record what is provided directly and what, if anything, is reimbursed later.",{"children":"Record what is provided directly and what, if anything, is reimbursed later."}],["$","li","Check when the first allowance payment would arrive.",{"children":"Check when the first allowance payment would arrive."}],["$","li","Keep a personal contingency appropriate to your own situation.",{"children":"Keep a personal contingency appropriate to your own situation."}],["$","li","Confirm travel dates and insurance requirements before accepting arrangements.",{"children":"Confirm travel dates and insurance requirements before accepting arrangements."}]]}],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
32:["$","section","5-A final five-question review",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-6","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"A final five-question review"}],[["$","p","Can you explain why this research environment fits a specific learning need? Does your actual study stage match the current eligibility wording? Do your proposed dates fit the chosen window? Has the required referee response arrived? Do you have evidence that the final application was submitted?",{"children":"Can you explain why this research environment fits a specific learning need? Does your actual study stage match the current eligibility wording? Do your proposed dates fit the chosen window? Has the required referee response arrived? Do you have evidence that the final application was submitted?"}],["$","p","If any answer is unknown, record the exact question and the official source or person who can answer it. A clear unresolved item is more useful than an invented green tick. This guide is an independent preparation aid; OIST makes the admission and placement decisions.",{"children":"If any answer is unknown, record the exact question and the official source or person who can answer it. A clear unresolved item is more useful than an invented green tick. This guide is an independent preparation aid; OIST makes the admission and placement decisions."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
